{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773929795,"nonce":"R5C6Tuzlzo29bxetK3U4WU1hFHU=","title":"Live issue sync: watcher re-dumps issue.json for reads, processes outbox for writes","message":"The container's StaticTracker reads issue.json once at startup and discards all write operations. Comments added to the issue after launch are invisible to the agent, and agent logs/checkpoints never reach the tracker.\n\n**Solution: bidirectional file-based sync**\n\n**Reads (host → container):**\n- Watcher re-dumps issue.json to the session dir on each loop iteration for active (working) sessions.\n- StaticTracker.reload() re-reads issue.json when mtime changes, returns new comments.\n- SessionRunner calls reload() between agent turns. New comments are injected into the agent's next prompt.\n\n**Writes (container → host):**\n- StaticTracker appends write operations to tracker-outbox.jsonl in /session/ instead of discarding them. Format: {\"op\": \"comment\", \"issue_id\": \"...\", \"text\": \"...\"}, {\"op\": \"label_add\", ...}, etc.\n- Watcher reads and processes the outbox each loop iteration, applying operations via the real GitBugTracker.\n- After processing, watcher truncates the file (or renames to .done).\n- The next re-dump of issue.json will include the newly posted comments, closing the loop.\n\n**Scope:**\n- adapters/trackers/static.py — reload() for reads, outbox writes instead of no-op\n- core/session.py — call reload() between turns, inject new comments\n- host/watcher/ — new module for outbox processing + periodic re-dump\n- host/issue_dump.py — re-dump support for running sessions\n- core/constants.py — filenames (TRACKER_OUTBOX_FILENAME)\n- Tests for each component\n\n**Not included:**\n- Replacing StaticTracker with a live tracker (keeps container sandboxed)\n- Real-time sync (polling interval is fine, ~30s delay acceptable)","files":null}]}